Create opens the port menu: controller navigation is on for this console.

The port menu - settings, controls, the input editor - opens from the pad's Create
button only while controller navigation is on, and that setting defaults to off
everywhere except the Switch and Wii U builds, which turn it on because a pad is all
they have. So is this console: without it a player holding only a pad can never
open the menu, since the other way in is Escape or F1 on a keyboard.

This registers the same default under `OOPS_TARGET`. It is a default, so a saved
setting still wins.

--- a/src/port/Engine.cpp
+++ b/src/port/Engine.cpp
@@ -630,7 +630,7 @@
     Instance->AudioInit();
     Instance->LoadDictionary();
     Instance->LoadPlayerAnims();
-#if defined(__SWITCH__) || defined(__WIIU__)
+#if defined(__SWITCH__) || defined(__WIIU__) || defined(OOPS_TARGET)
     CVarRegisterInteger(CVAR_IMGUI_CONTROLLER_NAV, 1); // always enable controller nav on switch/wii u
 #endif
     GhostshipGui::SetupGuiElements();
